  "description": "Construction of a front staircase with railings and a front lightwell",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;div style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;Following the removal of the existing tree hereby approved, a replacement tree shall be planted by one of the same species in the same vicinity, unless first agreed otherwise by the Local Planning Authority.&amp;nbsp; The replacement tree shall be planted during the planting season at the time of felling (end October - end March) or during the next immediately available planting season. The size of the tree shall be at least a Light Standard as per BS 3936-1:1992 (or any standard that reproduces or replaces this standard). The tree shall be maintained for 5 years after planting and should it be removed, die, be severely damaged or become seriously diseased within this period, it shall be replaced with another tree as originally required to be planted by this condition.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;REASON: In the interests of visual amenity, in accordance with Hackney Local Plan LP33; LP51 (adopted 2020) and pursuant to section 197 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
